From d1cbff7b45b8f9f6c1f4b2a758392e3182bfdff8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pdale-boop <237306950+pdale-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:06:55 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Fog: Wind Waker HD's curve, the square of the GameCube's
 linear fog, while the host has HD's distances in place

Wind Waker HD fogs every lit shader with clamp((d - start) / (end - start))^2 (the sea quad's PS 949 in the noon
capture at Windfall, the terrain's PS 1086 at night, Link's shader), and it retuned its palettes' fog distances for
that curve (noon 0 to 36,000, dawn -10,000 to 32,000). The host copies those distances into the GameCube's palettes
with HD's sky, where the game applies them on its linear GX fog: at noon an island 18,000 out took 0.50 of the fog
colour against HD's 0.25, and at dawn the scenery at the camera took 0.24 against 0.06.

aurora_set_fog_hd(1) sets a new shader key bit, ShaderKey::hd_fog (one of the pad bytes), on every draw with linear
fog, which then squares the clamped factor before the integer blend; the ubershader reads the bit from the key it is
given (now the draw's key with its per-draw bits, not the plan's). Off by default; unflagged modules are unchanged.

gxcore tests: the flagged module differs from the unflagged one by that line alone, the other curves are untouched,
and the ubershader reads the bit.

HD fogs its scenery after its light, by the distance from the eye (its room and
terrain shaders: mix(lit colour, fog, f), f the square of (distance - start) /
(end - start)). The draws fog by GX before the shade, so the sun pass shaded the
fog too: a dungeon room's far walls, in shade, lost most of HD's fog (Earth
Temple's teal, Hyrule Castle's warm haze). With dual-source blending the pass now
takes the draws' fog out (their GX fog, range adjust included, from
note_scene_fog) and puts HD's in after the shade: scene x keep + F x (fh - fs x
keep), in the scene's gamma as GX fogs. DOL_AURORA_SUN_FOG_HD=0 keeps it as drawn.

HD's fog starts before the camera in many places (Ganon's Tower -5000, the Wind Temple -5000, the Tower of the Gods
-1000, Cave01 -500), and the GameCube's palette blend (float_kankyo_color_ratio_set) clamps every blended value at
0, so the game fogged from 0 there: far less than HD (Ganon's Tower at 1000 units 0.012 against HD's 0.18).
aurora_set_fog_hd_starts: each frame the host gives HD's start for the palette blend in play (HD's entries' starts
blended as the game blends them, unclamped) with the game's end, and where the lit scenery's fog starts at 0 and its
end (the view depth over GX's ze) is that end, the sun pass fogs from HD's start. Wind Temple R0f goes from 0.76 to
0.97 of HD's brightness, Ganon's Tower's red share (after the lava glow) from 0.87 of HD's to 0.91.
